<title>NETHERLANDS: ING nine month results in detail.</title>
<headline>ING nine month results in detail.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of guilders)</p>
<p>INSURANCE INCOME</p>
<p>    - Life premiums			    11.531  vs 10.387</p>
<p>    - Non-life premiums			 5.462  vs  4.797</p>
<p>    - Investment income/other income	8.097  vs  6.903</p>
<p>INSURANCE PRE-TAX PROFITS</p>
<p>    - Life insurance			    0.845  vs  0.736</p>
<p>    - Non-life insurance			0.279  vs  0.240</p>
<p>    - General insurance			 0.596  vs  0.507</p>
<p>BANKING RESULTS</p>
<p>    - Net interest income		     5.212  vs  4.603</p>
<p>    - Securities/participations income    0.104  vs  0.089</p>
<p>    - Commission income:			1.979  vs  1.465</p>
<p>	-- funds transfer			 0.493  vs  0.476</p>
<p>	-- securities			     0.546  vs  0.345</p>
<p>	-- insurance broking		    0.080  vs  0.072</p>
<p>	-- other				    0.860  vs  0.592</p>
<p>    - Financial transaction income:	 0.936  vs  0.613</p>
<p>	-- securities trading		   0.725  vs  0.267</p>
<p>	-- forex dealing			  0.100  vs  0.171</p>
<p>	-- other				    0.111  vs  0.175</p>
<p>    - Other income				0.283  vs  0.256</p>
<p>    - Operating expenses			6.043  vs  4.934</p>
<p>- Value adjustments to receivables</p>
<p>	of banking operations		   0.850  vs  0.815</p>
<p>    - Pre-tax banking profit		  1.621  vs  1.277</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
